// CreatePlanWithBodyWithResponse Plan a maintenance job (dry run)
//
// Computes what the job would do (target set, effects) and stores the
// plan; apply it with `POST /admin/v1/jobs` before it expires. Kinds
// and roles: `scrub`, `quota_recalc`, `acl_reconcile`, `fts_rebuild`,
// `fts_dict_convert`, `fts_layout`, `mailbox_name_convert`,
// `attachment_backfill` (role `repair`), `mailbox_delete`, `expunge`,
// `purge` (role `delete`). `fts_layout` with `layout: 3` needs the
// cluster mark (`POST /admin/v1/fts/layout3/enable`), `fts_layout`
// with `dict_filter: ids` the cluster mark of the dictionary filter
// (`POST /admin/v1/fts/dictfilter/enable`), `fts_layout` and
// `fts_rebuild` with `online: true` the cluster mark of online runs
// (`POST /admin/v1/fts/online/enable`), `quota_recalc` with
// `online: true` the mark of online quota recounts (`POST
// /admin/v1/quota/online/enable`) and `mailbox_delete` with
// `online: true` the mark of the mailbox lock (`POST
// /admin/v1/mailbox/lock/enable`); without them the plan
// is refused with `conflict` (409). `fts_dict_convert` is a
// legacy kind for layout 2 indexes written before 0.35.0; for an
// account whose index has layout 3 it is refused with `conflict`
// (409). A plan that changes other accounts (ACL repairs, purge)
// needs them in the client scope. The account must be canonical.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /admin/v1/accounts/{account}/plans (the `CreatePlan` operationId).
